To stash all your current uncommitted changes:

```bash
git stash
```

This saves your changes and reverts the working directory back to the last commit. Then when you want to bring your changes back:

```bash
git stash pop
```

Other useful stash commands:

```bash
# See all stashes
git stash list

# Stash with a descriptive name
git stash push -m "font and icon size feature"

# Apply a specific stash without removing it from the list
git stash apply stash@{0}

# Drop a specific stash without applying it
git stash drop stash@{0}

# Clear all stashes
git stash clear
```

Note that `git stash pop` applies the most recent stash and removes it from the stash list, while `git stash apply` applies it but keeps it in the list.

